      "analysis_source": "llm-per-reviewer",
      "patch_summary": "This patch simplifies the rate limiting of version 1 events in the Linux kernel's memory cgroup (memcg) subsystem by collapsing multiple targets into a single counter. The target enum, per-cpu target array, and switch in memcg1_event_ratelimit() are all consolidated, eliminating the need for a node ID in memcg1_check_events(). This change reduces code complexity and makes maintenance easier."
